I've noticed quite a few people flaming others who complained about being
killed whilst overburdened:

"You can hardly move a handspan"-more-
The grid bug bites - you get zapped -more- ... ad nauseam and death

well, I stood on a great big pile and tried to pick up a potion and the
game nearly killed me. The reason? Well, it was the wrong pile - there was
no potion and I had asked to pick up !a (as I nearly always do). The game
says there are no ! here and promptly picks up everything else including
the 15 mordor orc corpses. Now I'd say that was a bug and a genuine reason
for complaint.

Always look at the options you're given and make sure you're stood on the
pile with the potion and not the one with over 300 pieces of armor - have
you shopped at Fort Ludios yet? What a laugh!

I disagree with the poster who suggested that the mines were too hard for
a starting character - they're perfect. A mini, self-contained dungeon with
plenty to kill, plenty to collect, shops, an altar and a useful little 'gray'
gem at the end. If your character can clear the Gnomish mines, you actually
stand a chance with the rest of the dungeon, all in under 10K moves.

I couldn't have believed that you could have made nethack easier to get into
but harder to play - well done to _everyone_ in the development team.

Mikes most excellent adventure!

